Chapter: FilesHoleTest
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Works chapter GopFiles
  cites Works chapter GopFat16
  cites Foreword chapter Fat16
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The Files open's durable part inside a real D.5 hole of `desk-files-want`
 bytes, the way `desk-files-open` runs it: the GPT lookup bracketed at the
 frontier first, then the mount and `desk-files-build` inside the hole, then
 the exit and the claim. An overrun would trap on the armed ceiling rather
 than print, so reaching the lines below is itself the fit; the room left is
 printed beside the verdict so the fit is a number.

 THE CONTROL IS THE FIRST LINE: an allocation taken before the hole is
 entered must not land in it, or the hole is only where allocations were
 going anyway. The last lines read the listing back through the state the
 hole holds, on the `files-window` fixture (a root of 22 entries).

Section: Body

  fh-yn : Boolean -> Text
  fh-yn (v) = if v then "PASS" else "FAIL"

Section: Main

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing =
    let ms = alloc-zeroed 128 64
    in let block = alloc-zeroed desk-files-want 64
    in let top = block + desk-files-want
    in let push = desk-marks-push ms desk-focus-files block
    in let kill = desk-marks-kill ms desk-focus-files
    in let outside = alloc-bytes 64
    in let g0 = __heap-save
    in act
    start <- gpt-esp-start
    let r = __heap-restore g0
    in let f0 = alloc-bytes 0
    in let i = desk-hole-enter ms top 0 desk-files-want
    in act
    m <- desk-files-mount start
    st <- desk-files-build (gapp-fallback (CbfFont { cbf-base = 0 })) m
    let cur = alloc-bytes 0
    in let claimed = desk-hole-exit ms i desk-focus-files
    in let f1 = alloc-bytes 0
    in act
    win <- gfl-window-cur (st.fs-vol) (st.fs-clusters) 0 3
    print-line-uni ("CONTROL, an allocation before the hole is outside it: " & fh-yn (outside < block | outside >= top))
    print-line-uni ("a dead span is picked: " & show i)
    print-line-uni ("the open allocated inside the hole: " & fh-yn (cur > block & cur < top))
    print-line-uni ("room left " & show (top - cur) & ", at least a page: " & fh-yn (top - cur >= 4096))
    print-line-uni ("the frontier is unmoved: " & fh-yn (f1 == f0))
    print-line-uni ("the entry is claimed for Files: " & fh-yn (desk-marks-id ms 0 == desk-focus-files & desk-span-reusable ms 0 top 0 == False))
    print-line-uni ("the mount held: " & fh-yn m.gm-ok)
    print-line-uni ("the state reads its count " & show (st.fs-count) & " and rows " & (list-at win 0).de-name & "," & (list-at win 1).de-name & "," & (list-at win 2).de-name & ": " & fh-yn (st.fs-count == 22 & list-length win == 3 & (list-at win 0).de-name == "EFI"))
    end
    end
    end
